# The alternative cost exiles "a blue card from your hand" (CR 118.9, 601.2b): Force of Negation cannot exile itself, so
# with only lands and itself in hand it is refused against Bot2's first Lightning Bolt (Bot1 takes 3). On turn 4 Bot1 has
# drawn a Brainstorm, a blue card, and exiles it to counter the second Bolt, which is exiled too: the control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Force of Negation
Island x6
Brainstorm
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x4
Mountain x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
! Bot1.Hand.Force of Negation.Cast(Stack.Lightning Bolt; Ability: exile a blue card)
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Life = 17
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Hand.Force of Negation.Cast(Stack.Lightning Bolt; Ability: exile a blue card)
Bot1.Choose(Brainstorm)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
Exile = Brainstorm; Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Graveyard = Force of Negation
